       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **Safety:** 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum recommended daily dose of ibuprofen. It could seriously harm the patient. The patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n- **Authorization:** A prescriber has to confirm the order, not someone in the finance office. I can't verify that a clinician has reviewed it.\n\n**What you can do:**\n- Ask the patient's prescriber to place or confirm the order. If they truly intend this dose, they can enter it themselves. The pharmacy will probably want to review it too.\n- If the dose was a mistake, have the prescriber give me the corrected dose. I can enter it once they do. For example, 800 mg by mouth three times daily is 2,400 mg/day.\n\nIf you tell me this was a transcription error and give me a prescriber's intended dose, I'm happy to help from there."
      }
